# NestJS Backend Module Style

Follow this structure and style when creating or updating anything in modules in `src/modules`.

## Module Structure

- Create: `*.module.ts`, `*.controller.ts` (follow nestjs-controller-generation.mdc rule), `*.service.ts` (follow nestjs-service-generation.mdc rule).
- Add folders: `dto/`, `entities/`, `filters/`, `response/`, `constants/`, `query-builders/` when needed.
- Keep file naming short and consistent: `create.dto.ts`, `update.dto.ts`, `params.dto.ts`, `<module>.entity.ts`, `<module>.filter.ts`, `<module>.response.ts`.
- When working with `*.dto.ts` files if needed (follow nestjs-dto-generation.mdc rule)
- When working with `*.filter.ts` files if needed (follow nestjs-filter-generation.mdc rule)
- When working with `*.response.ts` files if needed (follow nestjs-response-generation.mdc rule)

## Module File

- Provide repository class and service in `providers`.
- Export service from module.

## Database

- Never create any migration files for the database.
